  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Laser-patterned REBCO film on ~1 m cylindrical substrates can be manufactured at nuclear-grade quality and throughput, scaling from the demonstrated 6 T Helmholtz to 10 T nominal / 15-40 T peak coil fields",
      "A compact quasi-isodynamic stellarator at R ≤ 4 m, A ≈ 4, B = 10 T can achieve ignition (Q = ∞) with a 10 keV D-T plasma — an extrapolation with no stellarator experimental precedent at Q >> 1",
      "A flowing Li-LiH liquid metal wall can sustain 25 MW/m² continuous wall loading while serving as integrated first wall, breeder, shield, and coolant with stable MHD behavior in 3D stellarator geometry",
      "The optimized blanket (10 cm Pb + 22 cm non-enriched Li-LiH) achieves TBR = 1.60, providing ~39% margin above the 1.15 design requirement without Li-6 enrichment",
      "An sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine combined cycle can deliver 49-51% thermal cycle efficiency at GW scale from a liquid metal fusion heat source, yielding 34% net plant efficiency",
      "Steady-state ignited operation with NNBI used only for startup eliminates continuous heating/current-drive capital and recirculating load",
      "Tritium extraction from flowing Li-LiH at kg/day rates is achievable despite very high tritium solubility in liquid lithium"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "No central solenoid or current drive hardware — stellarator inherent, no CS fatigue cycling",
      "No plasma disruption mitigation hardware — enables higher capacity factor assumption",
      "No steady-state ECRH/gyrotron heating system — Q = ∞ target eliminates continuous heating capital and recirculating load",
      "No discrete solid first-wall replacement cycle — flowing liquid wall consolidates C220101/C220102 into a single pumped-fluid system",
      "No REBCO wound-tape supply chain bottleneck — laser-patterned film bypasses km-scale tape winding at $30-100/kA-m"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Industrial REBCO thin-film deposition and laser patterning at 1 m diameter cylindrical substrate scale — no manufacturing cost analogue at any scale (dominant LCOE uncertainty; 0.3×-10× coil cost scenario swing of ~418 $/MWh)",
      "Liquid Li-LiH circulation system — pumps, heat exchangers, tritium extraction, MHD conditioning piping at 25 MW/m² wall loading with no published cost analogue (Na-cooled fast reactor primary circuit used as structural lower bound)",
      "Liquid metal circulation pump power (~380 MW estimated) driving large unexplained recirculating power fraction (~32% of gross)",
      "Tritium-compatible heat exchangers between Li-LiH primary and sCO₂ secondary — permeation barriers with no demonstrated design",
      "sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine turbomachinery at ~1.5-2 GWe gross output — emerging technology with wide cost projection uncertainty at GW scale"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Entirely unanchored economics — no capital cost estimate, LCOE model, or CAS-level breakdown has been published by Renaissance Fusion or any independent third party",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Laser-patterned HTS film manufacturing cost has no industrial analogue; coil cost elasticity is +0.77 and the 10× scenario drives LCOE to 516 $/MWh",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "ISS04 confinement scaling extrapolated to the compact A≈4 geometry yields n·τ_E roughly 11× below the Lawson ignition threshold at T=10 keV — Q=∞ closure is not supported by current scaling laws",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "No stellarator has operated near burning plasma conditions; compact A ≈ 4 QI geometry has no experimental precedent and alpha confinement quality at ignition is untested",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Flowing Li-LiH wall at 25 MW/m² is unprecedented — MHD stability, plasma-facing free surface behavior, and tritium management in 3D stellarator geometry are uncharacterized",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "REBCO Jc degrades sharply above ~20 T at 20 K; achieving the 20-40 T peak coil field envelope with realistic current density is not addressed in available sources (b_max elasticity +0.38)",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Plant availability is the largest LCOE lever (elasticity -0.94) but maintenance intervals and component replacement schedules are entirely uncharacterized",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Liquid metal circulation pump power is not disclosed and drives the unexplained 18-percentage-point gap between 50% cycle efficiency and 34% net efficiency, preventing independent Q_engineering closure",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "sCO₂ Brayton-Rankine cycle at 49-51% efficiency has been demonstrated only at MW scale; GW-scale turbomachinery and integration with tritium-compatible heat exchangers are undemonstrated",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Divertor design and plasma exhaust solution is not addressed in any published source — critical gap for plasma-facing component cost and availability",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "RAFM structural steel qualification under combined Li-LiH chemical exposure and 14 MeV neutron irradiation at 25 MW/m² wall loading has not been demonstrated",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium permeation from flowing Li-LiH through heat exchanger walls to sCO₂ secondary is a documented concern with no published mitigation design",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "The sole hardware milestone (6 T Helmholtz, 1.2 m diameter, 20 K) is at 60% of nominal design field and does not characterize production economics or throughput",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Fission-style regulatory cost multiplier (Stewart & Shirvan 2.2× building costs) applies as upper-bound scenario for this D-T concept",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "D-T tritium startup requirement (~1 kg at >$35,000/g) subject to global inventory decline (~25-30 kg, 5.5%/year decay) and fleet sequencing constraint",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
